{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Good Leadership"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "To Give It Some Thought"}, {"type": "position", "content": 7}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 6}, {"type": "level", "content": "B2.3"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": " Describe the reasons or results of events or actions in spoken or written texts, in work and social contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Integrates factual information to a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge in the workplace."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Integrates factual information to a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge in the workplace."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Integrates factual information to a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge in the workplace."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Integrates factual information to a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge in the workplace."}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn11le06ob07re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "criticism"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "remarks that say what you think is bad about someone or something"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: They find it hard to deal with criticism. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le06ob07aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are words you use when talking about team oriented roles. "}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "novel"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "not like anything known before, and unusual or interesting"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I think their ideas are novel."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le06ob07aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "counter-productive"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "having an \u200beffect that is \u200bopposite to the one \u200bintended or \u200bwanted"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Since their ideas are novel, they may be considered counter-productive at times."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le06ob07aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "parameter"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a set of fixed limits that control the way that something should be done"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: They may be a poor communicator insofar as they tend to ignore given parameters."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le06ob07aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "constraint"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "something that limits your freedom to do what you want"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: We need to stay within these constraints. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le06ob07aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "shrewd"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "good at judging what people or situations are really like"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: It is said that they are shrewd and objective."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le06ob07aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "detached"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "not reacting to or becoming involved in something in an emotional way"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: They are often perceived as detached or unemotional."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le06ob07aud07"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to instigate "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to make something start"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: They react to events rather than instigating them. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le06ob07aud08"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "territorial"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "careful to guard what you consider to be your own, and prevent others from using it"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: They may come across as territorial."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le06ob07aud09"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "at the expense of"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "if you do one thing at the expense of another, doing the first thing \u200bharms the second thing:"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: They tend to be preoccupied with technicalities at the expense of the bigger picture."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le06ob07aud10"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Report Verbs with Impersonal Passive Constructions"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " You can use two different patterns with report verbs: Active and Passive."}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Active: <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">They say </span>that it rains a lot in London</span>. <br/> Passive: <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">It is said </span>that it rains a lot in London</span>."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You can also use the structure: <span class=\"italic\">It + passive report verb + finite clause</span> (a clause which can stand alone)."}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">It is thought</span> that the Pyramids took 25 years to build.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "This pattern is often used in formal reports, news reports and academic writing."}, {"type": "text", "content": "These are the verbs you can use with this structure: <br/> <span class=\"italic\">allege, announce, believe, claim, consider, declare, explain, feel, find, intend, know, mention, notice, object, observe, promise, prove, recommend, report, reveal, say, see, show, state, suggest, think, understand.</span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "It has been <span class=\"strong\">suggested </span>that they thrive on praise and find it hard to deal with criticism."}, {"type": "example", "content": "It is <span class=\"strong\">observed </span>that they prefer to work apart from the team. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "It is <span class=\"strong\">believed </span>that they carefully weigh the pros and cons before coming to a decision."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Reason Clauses Using <span class=\"italic\">in that, insofar as, inasmuch as, since</span> and <span class=\"italic\">as</span>"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " You introduce reason clauses with specific linking words. Each linking word or phrase carries its own meaning and use."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"underline\">since and as</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use <span class=\"italic\">since </span>and <span class=\"italic\">as </span>to introduce reasons that the listener or reader already knows."}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">Since </span>you've already completed your work, we can go for lunch. </span> <br/>  <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">As </span>you're new here, you should introduce yourself to everyone first.</span> "}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"underline\">in that, insofar as, inasmuch as</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use <span class=\"italic\">in that</span>, <span class=\"italic\">insofar </span>as and <span class=\"italic\">inasmuch as </span>to justify what we have just said by indicating by the statement is true. You use these words in fairly formal English."}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">She's a pleasure to work for, <span class=\"strong\">in that</span> she is attentive and motivating.</span> <br/>  <span class=\"italic\">We are expecting a busy week <span class=\"strong\">insofar as</span> all the appointments have been booked.</span> <br/> <span class=\"italic\">The employees are tired <span class=\"strong\">inasmuch as</span> they cannot work overtime.</span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Since their ideas are novel, they may be considered counter-productive at times. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "As they are fully committed to their field of expertise, they may come across as territorial. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Monitor-Evaluators are known to be good at analyzing in that they evaluate ideas."}, {"type": "example", "content": "They may be a poor communicator insofar as they tend to ignore given parameters and constraints. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "They are critical thinkers and very strategic inasmuch as that they are often perceived as detached"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Work in pairs."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Make a summary chart of all the team roles presented by Belbin."}, {"type": "text", "content": "In your chart include all nine role names, their positives contributions, and their allowable weaknesses."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Display the charts around the class and explain your chart."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I collaborate with a partner."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I analyze all the positive contributions and weaknesses of each role."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I create a summary chart that is interesting, easy to understand and informative."}]}], "labs": [{"type": "scholar", "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"type": "has_nav", "content": true}, {"type": "has_exercise_controls", "content": true}]}], "stimuli": [{"type": "welcome", "_data": [], "contents": [{}], "template_override": 1, "id": 0}, {"type": "audio", "title": "", "template_override": 1, "_data": [], "contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"images": [{"time": "", "image": "engenn11le06ob07re2img05.jpg", "text": "", "id": 0}, {"time": "10", "image": "engenn11le06ob07re2img05.jpg", "text": "Thought-Oriented Roles</br></br><ul><li> Plants come up with new ideas and approaches. It has been suggested that they thrive on praise and find it hard to deal with criticism. Often introverted, it is observed that they prefer to work apart from the team. Since their ideas are novel, they may be considered counter-productive at times. They may be a poor communicator insofar as they tend to ignore given parameters and constraints.", "id": 1}, {"time": "25000", "image": "engenn11le06ob07re2img06.jpg", "text": "<ul><li> Monitor-Evaluators are known to be good at analyzing in that they evaluate ideas that other people (often Plants) come up with. It is said that they are shrewd and objective. It is believed that they carefully weigh the pros and cons before coming to a decision. They are critical thinkers and very strategic inasmuch as that they are often perceived as detached or unemotional. However, it is agreed upon that they are poor motivators in that they react to events rather than instigating them.", "id": 2}, {"time": "52300", "image": "engenn11le06ob07re2img07.jpg", "text": "<ul><li> Specialists are dedicated and pride themselves on their skills and abilities. They possess specialized knowledge in a certain area. It is assumed that they provide the team with their knowledge and skills. They work hard to maintain their professional status. They are usually introverts and lack interest in other fields. As they are fully committed to their field of expertise, they may come across as territorial. They tend to be preoccupied with technicalities at the expense of the bigger picture.", "id": 3}], "audiosrc": "engenn11le06ob07re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn11le06ob07re2img05.jpg"}}], "id": 1}], "exercises": [{"type": "WLC", "img_path": "", "template_override": 1, "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I c